 "result": "The session cookie is written in `persist_session` as part of finalizing the response. In call order:\n\n1. `Tessel.finalize_request` (`src/tessel/app.py:1021`) turns the view's return value into a response with `make_response`, then calls `finalize_reply` at line 1041. It is reached from the dispatch method at line 1019, and from the error path at line 948.\n2. `Tessel.finalize_reply` (`src/tessel/app.py`, body at ~1395–1418) runs the `after_request` functions, then calls `persist_session` at line 1416 unless `is_null_session` is true. I inferred the method name from the call at line 1041. I did not read its `def` line.\n3. `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session` (`src/tessel/sessions.py:337`) does the actual write:\n   - It adds `Vary: Cookie` if the session was accessed.\n   - It calls `response.delete_cookie` if the session was modified to be empty (line 356).\n   - Otherwise it checks `cookie_needs_write` (`sessions.py:~234`, which also honours `SESSION_REFRESH_EACH_REQUEST`).\n   - It then signs the session with `make_signer(app).dumps(dict(session))` and calls `response.set_cookie(...)` (line 374).\n\nThe cookie attributes (domain, path, secure, samesite and so on) come from the `get_cookie_*` helpers in `sessions.py:172–221`, which read the `SESSION_COOKIE_*` config.",
